# Enforcement control plane — design §10.5 (publication-automation design), HUMAN-DECISIONS D15/D30.
# GitHub resolves the LAST matching pattern; every pattern below names the operator alone, so every
# control-plane path has exactly one code owner. Membership is defined by exact path in
# .github/control-plane-manifest.json; the four deny-by-default trees are listed first, then the
# governance documents and policy inputs outside those trees. Tests/automation/test_control_plane.py
# checks that every manifest path is effectively owned by the single owner named here.

# Deny-by-default trees (any file here is control plane; a new or renamed one is control plane
# from the moment it is added, and the same change must register it in the manifest — listing it
# records membership, it never removes it)
/.github/                                       @robertvitali
/scripts/                                       @robertvitali
/Tests/automation/                              @robertvitali
/bats/helpers/                                  @robertvitali

# Governance documents
/AGENTS.md                                      @robertvitali
/CLAUDE.md                                      @robertvitali
/HUMAN-DECISIONS.md                             @robertvitali
/docs/superpowers/specs/                        @robertvitali
/docs/runbooks/                                 @robertvitali
/docs/discovery/prelaunch-readiness-evidence.md @robertvitali

# Policy inputs read by in-plane drivers
/bats/tier-inventory.json                       @robertvitali
/docs/requirements.in                           @robertvitali
/docs/requirements.txt                          @robertvitali
/mkdocs.yml                                     @robertvitali
